        "id": "U5-D4",
        "statement": "A valid amount must match ^[0-9]\u002B(\\.[0-9]{1,2})?$ and be greater than 0. Signs, exponents, commas, a leading \u0027.\u0027 and a trailing \u0027.\u0027 are rejected with the new LendingError InvalidAmount (\u0027invalid amount \u0027x\u0027\u0027). The check lives in Tier 2 as Payments.PaymentAmount, whose constructor is private, so only parse can create one. The new error PaymentExceedsOwed renders as \u0027m1 owes only 1.50\u0027. Checks run in this order: unknown member, then invalid amount, then payment over what is owed. Paying more than is owed, including when the member owes 0.00, records nothing.",
